    "result_text": "The full build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe redesigned identity key and duplicate detection, per spec:\n\n**1. New `identityKey` formula** (`IdentityKeyNormalizer.java`)\nNow returns the lower-case hex **SHA-256** digest over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` \u2014 replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`. This satisfies the test's `[0-9a-f]{64}` shape check.\n\n**2. New `Soundex.java` utility**\nStandard American Soundex (retained first letter + up to three digits, zero-padded to 4; vowels/Y separate, H/W transparent). Self-contained \u2014 no new dependency added.\n\n**3. Duplicate detection = the single identity key** (`ClinicServiceImpl.java`)\n- Added `rejectWhenDuplicateIdentity(owner)`, which throws `DuplicateIdentityException` (\u2192 409) when the derived `identityKey` matches any **non-deleted** owner. The e-mail-domain blocklist still runs first (in the controller's `EmailNormalizer.normalize`, before the service is called).\n- Removed reliance on the old household-based 409 (there is now no separate household-duplicate block; `householdId` remains only for household member count / membership-level cap).\n\n**4. Soft match reworked** (`assignPossibleDuplicate`)\nNow sets `possibleDuplicate = true` (and `possibleDuplicateOf`) when the `identityKey` **differs** from an existing active owner but their `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match \u2014 so two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are created as a soft match rather than rejected.\n\nDocs on `DuplicateIdentityException`, `OwnerMapper`, and `ExceptionControllerAdvice` were updated to describe the new formula.\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical payload \u2192 409) both pass; full build SUCCESS.\n\nNote: this is not a git repository, so I've made no commits \u2014 the changes are in the working tree.",
